Changes made by FlashRT (2026-11-15)
  - Renamed model-port-workflow to vla-port-workflow. Rewrote the description
    and added Chinese trigger words.
  - Narrowed the scope. ApxInf ports whole LLM/VLM/VLA model families into
    ApxInf crates. FlashRT's port lane brings one method, kernel or backend
    into a FlashRT-native path for a given model, stage and GPU, and ends by
    handing off a snapshot candidate to the patch lane (vla-patch-candidate)
    with registry tool and stage ids.
  - Replaced the ApxInf required reading (doc/porting-workflow.md,
    adding-a-new-model.md, model-layer-architecture.md,
    model-execution-wiring.md, mlx-backend.md, adding-new-kernels.md) with
    FlashRT's documents:
      * docs/adding_new_model.md §0, §4.3 and §4.4;
      * docs/kernel_fusion.md and docs/kernel_catalog.md;
      * docs/vla_autotune.md;
      * the tool registry entry;
      * the vla-model-impl-map report.
  - Replaced the Rust module-ownership table (Model/Blocks, ModelRunner,
    weights, LlmTrait, VlaRuntime) with FlashRT placement: registry,
    frontend, pipeline_<hw>, csrc binding plus CMake gate, and the
    autotune-harness exclusion. Noted that an upstream source_dir sits
    outside snapshot identity.
  - Removed the MLX, CPU-reference, LLM chat-template and tuning-recipe
    specifics.
  - Kept the method:
      * a confirmed preflight tuple;
      * private reference capture;
      * semantic inventory;
      * the execution ledger (columns preserved);
      * coverage classification;
      * named scaffolds with exit criteria;
      * eager/graph parity, repeated replay, changed-input propagation,
        stable addresses and the host-transfer audit;
      * the functional versus optimization status split;
      * a product-only diff;
      * the hands-off/hands-on stop conditions;
      * "a partial foundation is not completion".
  - Added:
      * the operator gate (vla-operator-gate) for every new device path;
      * the kernel lane option;
      * snapshot build commands;
      * decision-log recording with an explicit actor;
      * the PatchProposal/candidate hand-off;
      * the current port and port-like registry tools (quant.int8_pi05,
        fusion.hy_rope_qknorm_kvwrite, cache.fastwam_text_crossattn_kv) with
